# Free Energy Mixer

Can log-sum-exp replace averaging in attention without costing you extra compute?

Published 2/10/2026 by Jiecheng Lu, Shihao Yang

## Overview

  * Free Energy Mixer addresses a fundamental problem in machine learning: how to properly combine predictions from multiple models or experts
  * Standard methods for mixing predictions lose information or produce distorted results
  * The paper proposes a new approach that preserves all relevant information when selecting among different models
  * The technique works by understanding what each model values and weighing their contributions accordingly
  * This matters because many modern systems rely on combining multiple specialized components

## Plain English Explanation

Imagine you have several experts giving you advice on different topics. One expert is great at finance, another at health, and another at technology. When you need an answer, you want to listen to the right expert for the job. But here's the catch: if you just ask each expert for their top recommendation and then average them together, you lose a lot of what they know. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
